+# What this fork will tell you before you trust it — DRAFT, NOT PUBLISHED
+
+> **Status: DRAFT.** Prepared by HQ seat-48, 2026-08-29, on HQ's D1 assignment. **Nothing here has
+> been published and nothing has been pushed.** This is the text proposed for the published fork's
+> README (or a `DISCLOSURE.md` beside it). It needs the President's word before it ships, and two of
+> its numbers move if the outstanding items below are closed first.
+
+Most forks tell you what they added. This one also tells you what it broke, what it has not
+measured, and where its own records were wrong. That is the point of the file.
+
+## 1. Run the provenance tool yourself — and know what it prints
+
+```
+python tools/arifi-sync/arifi_sync.py provenance
+```
+
+Today it exits **`FAIL: 27 commit(s) carry no provenance`** over 478 commits.
+
+**Read that number correctly.** Earlier records of this fork say 315. That figure was real, and it
+was an artifact: three base moves in one night (b10524 → b10636 → b10680) rebased the branch and
+rewrote every sha, which killed all 289 keys of the fork's own grandfather ledger. The content was
+never lost — 289 of 289 ledger subjects still matched a commit exactly once — but the key was dead,
+so the tool counted audited native work as unprovenanced. The ledger was re-keyed by subject match
+on 2026-08-29 and the count fell to its true value.
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| commits in range | 478 |
+| `Taken-from`/`Origin` STRICT (git's own parser — what CI sees) | 149 |
+| LOOSE (token present anywhere in the message) | 161 |
+| `Measured-effect` present | 122 |
+| native `Origin` trailer | 28 |
+| grandfathered native (sha-pinned ledger) | 289 |
+| **no provenance** | **27** |
+
+The 27 are fork-native commits made after the `Origin: ArifiLabs (native)` convention was minted on
+2026-08-20 and before it was enforced. The convention was written down and then not applied. That
+is a bookkeeping backlog, not an attribution claim, and it is named rather than closed by hand.
+
+## 2. The attribution claim this fork does NOT yet make
+
+**The grandfather ledger has not been audited against the commits it classifies.** It calls 289
+commits "fork-authored, no upstream origin exists". 180 of them have a patch-filename subject naming
+work that is manifestly not fork-authored — ports from TurboQuant, laguna, ROCmFPX, and upstream
+pull requests by number. Six of those subjects end in an upstream PR number, and **all six resolve
+to real merged commits in `ggml-org/llama.cpp`.**
+
+Two things follow, and they are different sizes:
+
+- **License exposure: none from those six.** Upstream llama.cpp is this fork's own base and its own
+  MIT licence; carrying upstream commits is not an unattributed take.
+- **The ledger's claim is still wrong for them**, and "fork-authored" is precisely the claim that
+  suppresses an attribution requirement. Until the remaining commits are re-audited against their
+  diffs, **this fork does not claim its attribution is complete** — and that claim is the whole
+  point of shipping the provenance tooling next to the code.
+
+A green `grandfathered NATIVE` count is not evidence that attribution is complete. It means the key
+resolves.
+
+## 3. Known-wrong numbers, still on the record
+
+- **The Escha `gsm8k` cell of 0.140 is superseded and has no replacement yet.** It was 90% empty
+  strings, not a reasoning result: a think-native ChatML model handed a raw base-LM few-shot block
+  emits EOS at position 0. The defect is fixed and proven gone (45/50 empty → 0 empty across 26
+  completions); the rerun stopped at 30/50, so the corrected score does not exist. Treat 0.140 as
+  superseded wherever it appears.
+- **43 commits carry `Measured-effect: UNMEASURED`.** That is the honest word, not a gap — the
+  trailer exists so an unmeasured take cannot pass as measured. It includes the CUDA and Metal
+  TQ3_4S kernel lifts, which are **built on no machine here**; this estate is Vulkan-only.
+- **Six commits carry `Taken-from:` with no `Measured-effect:` trailer at all** — absent, not
+  UNMEASURED: `f4c4a2aa6`, `21c246c65`, `28cc9baf5`, `cc4cdce31`, `c0e373068`, `690b0340a`.
+- **Eleven commits carry provenance that is human-readable but not machine-readable**, because a
+  trailer value wrapped to column 0 and git ends the trailer block at the first non-trailer-shaped
+  line — invalidating every trailer above it too. They are disclosed, not fixed: fixing them means
+  rewriting the branch, which this project's own runbook forbids the tools for.
+
+## 4. What a user on other hardware is NOT getting
+
+This rig is a single Vulkan iGPU (AMD Radeon 780M, gfx1103). Two consequences are structural:
+
+- **Off-rig backend content is deliberately dropped in conflicting hunks.** Both 2026-08-29 base
+  moves applied a path-scoped policy keeping the fork's side for CUDA / Metal / SYCL / HIP and
+  `.github/workflows`, because those files are never built, swept or benched here. Stated plainly:
+  **a CUDA user is not getting upstream's b10524 → b10680 deltas to those files.** Per-hunk log:
+  `04b-auto-offrig-log.tsv`.
+- **Twelve off-rig backend rows landed BUILD-UNPROVEN**, by ruling, with their shas named in the
+  turboquant `pin_review`.
+
+## 5. An open non-determinism, and what it invalidates
+
+**MoE decode on Vulkan is non-deterministic at temperature 0 / top_k 1, and it is not this fork's
+regression.** Five fork runs of Ornith-1.5 at `-ngl 999` all differ — and so do three runs of
+**stock upstream b10636**. No deterministic reference exists on this architecture.
+
+The consequence a reader must be told: an earlier finding of this fork — "speculative decoding
+changed the model's output versus plain" — **was never controlled**, because plain-versus-plain
+diverges the same way. Dense 27B is unaffected on record. Status: filed, no fix, no guard.
+
+## 6. Pre-existing debt, re-confirmed and not introduced by the recent moves
+
+Several mid-series commits carry literal `<<<<<<< ours` / `>>>>>>> theirs` markers in committed
+source: **a user who checks out a mid-series patch gets a tree that does not compile.** A later
+series commit removes them and the **tip is marker-free** (0 hits outside `patches/`, re-scanned at
+b10680). Separately, `src/models/dflash.cpp` carries the DSV4 hparams block twice, the second dead
+after the first returns — present before and after the move.
+
+## 7. Long context: what is met and what is not
+
+**131,072 tokens is met. 200K is not.** At `-ub 256` the fork prefilled 127,488 tokens and decoded
+6.16 t/s at full context. **At the seated `-ub 512` it dies at ~74k.** The 100K+ claim is true only
+with the smaller ubatch, and the seated configuration does not carry it.
+
+## 8. Every source this fork carries code or credit from
+
+Nine projects, each with a retained verbatim notice in `licenses/`: `ggml-org/llama.cpp`,
+`Tiiny-AI/PowerInfer` (+ `smallthinker`), `PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp`, `charlie12345/ROCmFPX`,
+`llama-cpp-turboquant`, `turboquant_plus`, `turbo-tan/llama.cpp-tq3`, `thecodacus/llama.cpp`,
+`spiritbuun/buun-llama-cpp`, plus `ciru-ai/ROCmFPX` and `LaurentZuijdwijk/llama.cpp` registered
+ahead of ingest. `licenses/README.md` records the one real historical gap **as a gap** — a
+controller ingested on 2026-08-21 whose notice was not retained until 2026-08-27, six days later,
+stated rather than hidden.
+
+---
+
+## Before this ships — the numbers that move
+
+1. **The G12 re-audit** (§2). If it runs, §2 is rewritten from "not claimed" to a verdict.
+2. **The gsm8k rerun** (§3, ~1.6 h of quiet GPU). If it runs, 0.140 gets a replacement instead of a
+   supersession notice.
+3. **The `Origin` convention ruling.** If the convention binds, §1's 27 are a live backlog with a
+   forward gate; if it is retired, §1 loses its last paragraph.
